7106 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 7107 0 R/Alt(Plot of frequency omega over omega_ac, from 0 to 3.2, against horizontal wave number c_s k_x over omega_ac, from 0 to 3, for Gamma equal to 5/3. The upper curve, solid, starts at omega equal to omega_ac at k_x equal to 0, stays flat until about c_s k_x equal to omega_ac, then rises and approaches the line omega equal to c_s k_x. The region above it is shaded and labelled acoustic waves (p-modes). The lower curve, dashed, starts at 0, rises along the line omega equal to c_s k_x, and levels off just below 1, at the buoyancy frequency N, which is about 0.98 omega_ac. The region below it is shaded and labelled gravity waves (g-modes). Horizontal lines mark omega_ac and N. A dotted diagonal line, omega equal to c_s k_x, labelled Lamb wave, runs through the unshaded band between the two curves.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[208]/Pg 20547 0 R>>
endobj
