7365 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 7366 0 R/Alt(Logarithmic plot of the pressure ratio p_2/p_1 against the volume ratio V_2/V_1 for Gamma = 5/3. The adiabats p V^Gamma = const are straight blue lines. The shock adiabat, in black, touches the adiabat through the point (1, 1) at that point. For compressions, V_2/V_1 < 1, it rises above it towards a vertical asymptote at V_2/V_1 = (Gamma - 1)/(Gamma + 1) = 1/4, and a compressed state lies on a higher adiabat, so its entropy is larger. For expansions, V_2/V_1 > 1, the shock adiabat is dashed and lies below the adiabat through (1, 1), so the entropy would be smaller.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[46]/Pg 20552 0 R>>
endobj
